  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Municipality&#x2011;level Needs Assessment of Sudanese Nationals in High&#x2011;density Hubs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the outbreak of armed conflict in Sudan in April 2023, Libya has experienced a sustained increase in the arrival of Sudanese nationals. Through this project, IOM is conducting a needs assessment (NA) for Sudanese in Libya to strengthen evidence-based interventions in Libya. The NA is being carried out by the Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) and Research Unit at IOM Libya, in close coordination with IOM Libya&apos;s medical teams, for whom the assessment can help further tailor programmatic interventions. In doing so, IOM Libya will ensure that humanitarian/development actors have access to evidence-based data and analysis on Sudanese needs in high-density municipalities in Libya.</narrative>
  </description>
